            "review_text": "Soulman1949\nManchester, United Kingdom57 contributions\n0\nCheap and cheerful Viet food in Hanoi\nMar 2017 • Couples\nMon Ngon 24 is located right in the heart of the Old Quarter, a few minutes walk from Hanoi Cathedral at 24 Lý Quốc Sư. It seems to aim for the cheap and cheerful end of the foreign travel trade, serving Vietnamese food. The location is very busy with lots of passing trade and there is a steady flow of customers.\n\nA good selection of food is available and the service was pretty good. The food is OK but not spectacular, which probably describes the place pretty much. There are loads of places like this without any special characteristic that makes them stand out. So it's not bad but nothing special. If you're looking for a cheap and cheerful pit-stop then this place is fine. If you're looking for something \"a little bit more\" then look elsewhere.\n\nWe went on a Thursday evening and the place was full throughout. Most of the clientele are young and on a budget.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 4, 2017",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
